Package: linwas
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Mehmed Gürbüz <mehmedgrbz11@gmail.com>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libstdc++6 (>= 11), libegl1, libgl1, libfontconfig1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libdbus-1-3, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xkb1, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: network-manager, rsync, libhivex-bin
Suggests: timeshift, flatpak
Homepage: https://github.com/mehmedgur/linwas
Description: Linux assistant for people coming from Windows
 Linwas, Windows'tan geçenlerin Linux'u terminal kullanmadan yönetmesini
 sağlar: programlar, güncellemeler, sürücüler, ayarlar ve sorun giderme.
 .
 Linwas helps people who switch from Windows to manage a Debian/Ubuntu based
 Linux system without using the terminal: software, updates, drivers,
 settings and troubleshooting.
 .
 This package bundles its own Python runtime and Qt (PySide6).
